[1marray-bag[0m  [2mbackend/value-objects[0m
  String-indexing (`$arr['key']`) a structured array param instead of giving it a name —
  the type was never defined.

[33mWhy it is a sin[0m

  Data that travels together is a **thing**, not a loose pile of arrays and primitives.
  The moment a
  cluster of values is passed around, returned, or reached into by string keys, it wants a
  name and a type.

[33mHow to fix it[0m

  Give a structured array a typed value object — never read a named field by string key
  off an `array` param.
  A Spatie `Data` object built via `::from($array)`.

[33mExample[0m

  ```php
  ----------[ Bad ]----------
  
  public function normalize(array $row): void
  {
      $this->products->upsert(
          $row['sku'] ?? '',
          $row['name'] ?? '',
          (int) ($row['stock'] ?? 0),
      );
  }
  
  ----------[ Good ]----------
  
  // in Shop\Catalog\ImportRowNormalizer
  // The same import row, given its type the moment it arrives: `ImportRow::from($row)` names the
  // fields ONCE at the boundary, so nothing downstream reads `$row['sku']` off a loose array.
  
  public function ingest(array $row): void
  {
      $this->persist(ImportRow::from($row));
  }
  
  // The same row with its required fields non-nullable: `::from()` fails hard on a
  // real miss, so a valid row can't be confused with a malformed one.
  
  final class ImportRow extends Data
  {
      public function __construct(
          public readonly string $sku,
          public readonly int $quantity,
          public readonly ?int $priceCents = null,
          public readonly ?string $note = null,
      ) {}
  
      public function lineTotal(): int
      {
          return $this->quantity * ($this->priceCents ?? 0);
      }
  }
  ```

[33mCommands[0m

  [36mLearn     [0m load the skill [1mcommandments-backend-value-objects[0m
  [36mExempts   [0m commandments exemptions array-bag
  [36mFind it   [0m commandments judge --sin=array-bag
  [36mTurn off  [0m commandments disable array-bag
  [36mWrong?    [0m commandments report --detector=ArrayBagDetector --reason="…" --ref=PATH:LINE


